    {
      "finding": "Current-session capability, schema, and OpenAPI expectations still described response schema version 1.",
      "resolution": "Advanced every producer and consumer to strict schema version 2 and added closed regression expectations."
    },
    {
      "finding": "A command for a non-selected site could reach idempotency lookup before selected-site denial.",
      "resolution": "Snapshot authority now requires the requested site to equal the server-selected site before command lookup, returning a closed authorization denial."
    },
    {
      "finding": "Locking the previous immutable event with FOR SHARE required UPDATE row-policy visibility and hid the prior hash from the function-only identity role.",
      "resolution": "The exact session row remains locked for the full transition and serializes the per-session chain; the immutable prior event is read without an unnecessary row lock under its exact historical site scope."
